[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-net.cxd — the wire's page,
   repo-cx-platform-net.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 3).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the net
   suite). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-net
  [intro
    """Every socket in CX is opened here, and none opens without
       your say-so. `cx-platform-net` is the wire: stream and datagram
       transports, TLS on either side, name resolution, and the HTTP/1.1
       server that everything served on this site listens with. Every verb
       that touches the network is behind the `net` grant, and a denial is a
       value naming the flag that would allow it."""]
  [body
    """An address is a value before it is a socket. `parse-addr` reads a
       restricted transport URL or a bare `host:port` into an `[addr]`
       element — host, port, family, scheme — and refuses what a URL parser
       would happily carry into a dial: user information, a query, a path on
       a stream scheme, an unbracketed IPv6 literal. The corpus grades each
       refusal by name beside the round trips, so an address that reaches
       `dial` or `listen` is one the program could have inspected first."""]
  [body
    """The `net` grant gates the effects, not the arithmetic: resolve, dial,
       listen, accept, every read and write, and the datagram pair are each
       refused without it — one case per verb — and `http` adds no
       capability of its own. The server is an accept loop over a handler
       that maps a request to a response, with Server-Sent Events for
       held-open push and the WebSocket handshake graded frame by frame;
       what it serves and how a deployment runs it is the [[operations]]
       page. The `ftp` and `sftp` rows the registry carries are planned, and
       the table below shows only what ships today."""]
  [gives
    """Two modules of the platform group: the transport layer and the HTTP
       server built over it. Each links to the reference page the guide
       projects from the module's own documentation; the transports the
       store, the fabric and the application host speak over are these."""]
  [try
    """A transport URL parsed into an address value — the host, the port and
       the family, as an element a program can pattern-match before anything
       is dialed. Nothing here needs a grant."""]
  [fixture id=net-001-parse-addr-tcp]
  [status
    """The wire builds on the language and is built on by mail, identity,
       the store, the fabric and the application host; the front door
       compiles its V module from the pin."""]]
